      "body": "**Actionable comments posted: 8**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (5)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>.gitignore (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`29-30`: _⚡ Quick win_\n\n**`storybook-static` ignore 범위를 루트 기준으로 좁히는 걸 권장합니다.**\n\n현재 `storybook-static` 규칙은 리포지토리 어느 위치에 있든 `storybook-static` 디렉토리/파일을 무시할 수 있어요. 보통 Storybook 빌드 산출물은 루트에 생기므로 `/storybook-static/` 처럼 루트 한정이 안전합니다.\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-*storybook.log\n-storbybook-static\n+*storybook.log\n+/storybook-static/\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.gitignore around lines 29 - 30, 현재 .gitignore의 \"storybook-static\" 패턴은 리포지토리\n전체에서 해당 이름의 폴더/파일을 무차별적으로 무시하므로, 루트에 생성되는 빌드 산출물만 무시하도록 패턴을 루트 기준으로 좁히세요;\n.gitignore에서 \"storybook-static\" 항목을 찾아 \"/\" 접두사와 \"/\" 접미사로 루트 디렉토리 한정 패턴으로 변경하고(예:\n/storybook-static/), 기존 \"*storybook.log\" 등 다른 패턴은 그대로 둡니다.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>src/common/components/Title/Title.tsx (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`3-11`: _⚡ Quick win_\n\n**제목 컴포넌트는 heading 태그로 의미론을 보강해 주세요.**\n\nLine 3의 `styled.span`은 시각적으로는 제목이지만 문서 구조상 제목으로 인식되지 않습니다. 스크린리더/키보드 탐색 개선을 위해 heading 요소를 사용하는 편이 좋습니다.  \n \n\n<details>\n<summary>제안 코드</summary>\n\n```diff\n-const StyledTitle = styled.span`\n+const StyledTitle = styled.h2`\n+  margin: 0;\n   font-size: 18px;\n   font-weight: 700;\n   color: `#000`;\n `;\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@src/common/components/Title/Title.tsx` around lines 3 - 11, The StyledTitle\nis currently a styled.span causing headings not to be semantic; change\nStyledTitle to render a heading element (e.g. styled.h1/h2/h3) or make it a\nstyled component that accepts a variant/level prop and renders the appropriate\nheading tag, then update the Title component to use that heading element (retain\nthe StyledTitle name and styling) so the Title({value}) returns a semantic\nheading (e.g. <StyledTitle> becomes an <h2> by default or controlled via prop)\nto improve accessibility for screen readers and document structure.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>src/common/types/CardInfoType.ts (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-11`: **`cardNumbers`를 고정 길이 튜플 타입으로 좁혀야 합니다.**\n\nLine 2의 `string[]` 타입은 가변 길이를 허용하지만, 실제 코드는 카드 번호 4슬롯을 고정으로 가정합니다. `CardRegisterPage.tsx`에서 초기화할 때 `['', '', '', '']`로 4개를 설정하고, `CardNumberDisplay.tsx`와 `NumberField.tsx`에서도 모두 4개 인덱스를 전제로 동작합니다. 타입을 `[string, string, string, string]`으로 좁혀서 컴파일 타임에 도메인 제약을 명시하면 타입 안정성이 향상됩니다.\n\n<details>\n<summary>제안 위치</summary>\n\n```ts\n// src/common/types/CardInfoType.ts Line 1-5\nexport type CardInfoType = {\n  cardNumbers: [string, string, string, string];  // string[] → 튜플 타입으로 변경\n  expiryMonth: string;\n  expiryYear: string;\n};\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@src/common/types/CardInfoType.ts` around lines 1 - 11, The CardInfoType\ncurrently declares cardNumbers as string[] which allows variable length; change\nit to a fixed tuple type [string, string, string, string] and update\nCardInfoHandlersType.setCardNumbers to accept that same tuple type so the type\nsystem enforces four slots; then update all related usages (e.g., initializers\nin CardRegisterPage, accesses in CardNumberDisplay and NumberField, and any\nfunctions that call setCardNumbers) to use and pass the\n[string,string,string,string] tuple instead of a generic string[].\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>src/feature/CardRegister/components/InfoInputSection/InfoInputSection.tsx (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`22-24`: _⚡ Quick win_\n\n**렌더링 중 `console.log` 디버그 출력은 제거하는 게 좋습니다.**\n\nLine 22~24는 에러 상태에서 매 렌더마다 로그가 찍혀 노이즈를 만듭니다.  \n \n\n<details>\n<summary>변경 제안</summary>\n\n```diff\n-  if (isError) {\n-    console.log('error');\n-  }\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@src/feature/CardRegister/components/InfoInputSection/InfoInputSection.tsx`\naround lines 22 - 24, Remove the noisy console.log in InfoInputSection.tsx:\ndelete the if (isError) { console.log('error'); } block and, if you need to\nrecord the error, either show a user-facing error message in the component\nrender or log it once in an effect (e.g., useEffect(() => { if (isError)\nlogger.error(error) }, [isError])) so that the boolean isError check no longer\ncauses a console print on every render.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>src/common/components/Input/Input.tsx (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`32-33`: _⚡ Quick win_\n\n**오류 상태를 `aria-invalid`로도 노출해 주세요.**\n\n현재는 테두리 색상만 바뀌어서 보조기기 입장에서 오류 상태가 전달되지 않습니다.  \n \n\n<details>\n<summary>변경 제안</summary>\n\n```diff\n const Input = ({strokeMode = 'default', type = 'text', ...rest}: InputPropsType) => {\n-  return <StyledInput $strokeMode={strokeMode} type={type} {...rest} />;\n+  return (\n+    <StyledInput\n+      $strokeMode={strokeMode}\n+      type={type}\n+      aria-invalid={rest['aria-invalid'] ?? (strokeMode === 'error')}\n+      {...rest}\n+    />\n+  );\n };\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@src/common/components/Input/Input.tsx` around lines 32 - 33, The Input\ncomponent currently only changes visual stroke via StyledInput but does not\nexpose error state to assistive tech; update the Input function to set\naria-invalid on the rendered element (StyledInput) based on strokeMode (e.g.,\naria-invalid={strokeMode === 'error'}) while still allowing a passed-in\naria-invalid in ...rest to override if provided; modify the Input component (and\nensure StyledInput accepts arbitrary aria-* props) so screen readers receive the\nerror state.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for all review comments with AI agents</summary>\n\n````\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nInline comments:\nIn `@README.md`:\n- Line 158: The README's folder tree shows \"CvCField.tsx\" but the actual\ncomponent file is named \"CvcField.tsx\", causing a case/ordering mismatch; update\nthe README entry to \"CvcField.tsx\" (or alternatively rename the source file to\nmatch the README) so the displayed filename exactly matches the real symbol\nCvcField.tsx to avoid confusion when navigating the docs.\n- Line 121: The fenced code block start token (```) in the README's code sample\nis missing a language tag; update the opening fence to include an appropriate\nlanguage identifier (e.g., add \"bash\" or \"text\" after the ``` that begins the\ncode block) so markdownlint warnings are resolved and syntax highlighting works\ncorrectly.\n\nIn `@src/common/components/Label/Label.tsx`:\n- Around line 9-11: Change the Label component to accept an optional htmlFor\nprop and forward it to the rendered label element: update the Label props (for\nexample in the Label function signature) to include htmlFor?: string alongside\nvalue: string, and pass that htmlFor into <StyledLabel\nhtmlFor={htmlFor}>{value}</StyledLabel> so the label can be explicitly\nassociated with its input.\n\nIn\n`@src/feature/CardRegister/components/CardPreviewSection/CardBrandLogo/CardBrandLogo.tsx`:\n- Line 10: The BrandLogoImg image is missing an alt attribute which prevents\nassistive tech users from learning the card brand; update the CardBrandLogo\ncomponent to pass a meaningful alt string to BrandLogoImg (e.g., based on\nbrandName like \"Visa card logo\" or \"Mastercard logo\") and ensure the prop is set\nwhen rendering in the return expression that currently chooses between visaImg\nand masterCardImg.\n\nIn\n`@src/feature/CardRegister/components/CardPreviewSection/CardPreviewContainer/CardPreviewContainer.tsx`:\n- Around line 15-16: The current brand detection in CardPreviewContainer uses\nprefix = Number(fullNumber.slice(0, 2)) and only checks 51–55, so MasterCard\n2-series (2221–2720) are missed; modify the logic to also parse the first 4\ndigits (e.g., const prefix4 = Number(fullNumber.slice(0,4))) and add a check\nthat returns 'masterCard' when prefix4 is between 2221 and 2720 (in addition to\nthe existing 51–55 check on prefix), ensuring you evaluate the 4-digit range\nbefore or alongside the 2-digit check using the fullNumber and prefix/prefix4\nvariables.\n\nIn\n`@src/feature/CardRegister/components/InfoInputSection/ExpiryField/ExpiryField.stories.tsx`:\n- Around line 41-42: Interactive story local state is initialized from args but\nnever updated when Controls change; update the story to sync local state with\nincoming args by watching args.expiryMonth and args.expiryYear and calling\nsetExpiryMonth/setExpiryYear (or remove local state and read args directly) so\nControls changes reflect immediately; target the useState lines for\nexpiryMonth/expiryYear and add a useEffect that updates those states when args\nchanges.\n\nIn\n`@src/feature/CardRegister/components/InfoInputSection/ExpiryField/ExpiryField.tsx`:\n- Around line 86-95: updateErrorInfo currently updates shared overall error\nstate via setIsError using only this field's result, which can overwrite other\nfields' errors; instead remove the local setIsError update and report this\nfield's boolean up to the parent so the parent aggregates per-field errors.\nModify updateErrorInfo to only update local errorInfo (flag/currentErrorMsg) and\ncall a provided prop callback (e.g., setFieldError or similar) with the field\nkey \"expiry\" and hasError; then update the parent (InfoInputSection) to maintain\na fieldErrors map (number/expiry/cvc) and compute isError =\nObject.values(fieldErrors).some(Boolean). Ensure the function name\nupdateErrorInfo and props setFieldError/fieldErrors are used so changes are easy\nto find.\n\nIn `@src/styles/reset.css`:\n- Around line 11-24: The reset file mixes global reset with app layout rules:\nremove the min-height/height on html, body, `#root` and the body\nflex/centering/line-height/font-smoothing layout rules from src/styles/reset.css\nso the reset only normalizes browser defaults; instead add those layout rules to\na page container component (e.g., .page-container or App root component styles)\nand apply centering/100vh where a specific screen needs it; update references to\nhtml, body, `#root` in Reset to only include neutral resets and move the\ndisplay:flex, justify-content, align-items, and height declarations into the\ncomponent/style that renders the main page container.\n\n---\n\nNitpick comments:\nIn @.gitignore:\n- Around line 29-30: 현재 .gitignore의 \"storybook-static\" 패턴은 리포지토리 전체에서 해당 이름의\n폴더/파일을 무차별적으로 무시하므로, 루트에 생성되는 빌드 산출물만 무시하도록 패턴을 루트 기준으로 좁히세요; .gitignore에서\n\"storybook-static\" 항목을 찾아 \"/\" 접두사와 \"/\" 접미사로 루트 디렉토리 한정 패턴으로 변경하고(예:\n/storybook-static/), 기존 \"*storybook.log\" 등 다른 패턴은 그대로 둡니다.\n\nIn `@src/common/components/Input/Input.tsx`:\n- Around line 32-33: The Input component currently only changes visual stroke\nvia StyledInput but does not expose error state to assistive tech; update the\nInput function to set aria-invalid on the rendered element (StyledInput) based\non strokeMode (e.g., aria-invalid={strokeMode === 'error'}) while still allowing\na passed-in aria-invalid in ...rest to override if provided; modify the Input\ncomponent (and ensure StyledInput accepts arbitrary aria-* props) so screen\nreaders receive the error state.\n\nIn `@src/common/components/Title/Title.tsx`:\n- Around line 3-11: The StyledTitle is currently a styled.span causing headings\nnot to be semantic;